<!-- Compact homepage FAQ accordion (full-width) -->
<section id="faq" class="py-5 cf-faq-fullbleed">
  <div class="cf-faq-accordion">
    <div class="cf-faq-list">
      <details class="cf-faq-item" data-id="q1">
        <summary>
          What is CogniFocus?
          <span class="cf-faq-toggle" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
        </summary>
        <div class="cf-faq-body">
          <div class="cf-faq-content">
            CogniFocus is an Android focus timer with Shield blocking, Manual
            Block, Planned Sessions, Goblin reactions, and recovery nudges.
            It is built for people who want a session that pushes back when
            attention drifts instead of just counting down.
          </div>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="cf-faq-item" data-id="q2">
        <summary>
          How does Shield work during focus sessions?
          <span class="cf-faq-toggle" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
        </summary>
        <div class="cf-faq-body">
          <div class="cf-faq-content">
            During an active session, Shield watches for blocked apps and
            interrupts them before the scroll takes over. The Goblin reacts,
            and the session pulls you back toward the work instead of leaving
            you in the distraction loop.
          </div>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="cf-faq-item" data-id="q3">
        <summary>
          What is Manual Block?
          <span class="cf-faq-toggle" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
        </summary>
        <div class="cf-faq-body">
          <div class="cf-faq-content">
            Manual Block lets you block selected apps outside a focus session.
            Use it when you want direct protection for study time, bedtime, or
            any other window where you do not want distractions open at all.
          </div>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="cf-faq-item" data-id="q4">
        <summary>
          What are Planned Sessions?
          <span class="cf-faq-toggle" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
        </summary>
        <div class="cf-faq-body">
          <div class="cf-faq-content">
            Planned Sessions are focus blocks you schedule ahead of time. They
            are useful when you want recurring reminders and a session that is
            already waiting for you instead of starting from scratch each day.
          </div>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="cf-faq-item" data-id="q5">
        <summary>
          What happens if I pause or slip?
          <span class="cf-faq-toggle" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
        </summary>
        <div class="cf-faq-body">
          <div class="cf-faq-content">
            Pausing temporarily stops the session. If you slip into a blocked
            app, recovery nudges help you come back without losing the whole
            run. The Goblin keeps it honest, but one bad moment does not have
            to end the session.
          </div>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="cf-faq-item" data-id="q6">
        <summary>
          Why does it need Android permissions?
          <span class="cf-faq-toggle" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
        </summary>
        <div class="cf-faq-body">
          <div class="cf-faq-content">
            Usage Access lets CogniFocus see which app is in front so Shield
            can react. Display over other apps lets the Shield screen appear.
            Those permissions are used for focus protection, not for reading
            your content.
          </div>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="cf-faq-item" data-id="q7">
        <summary>
          What does CogniFocus not read?
          <span class="cf-faq-toggle" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
        </summary>
        <div class="cf-faq-body">
          <div class="cf-faq-content">
            CogniFocus does not read your messages, contacts, passwords, or the
            text inside your apps. It uses the app-in-front signal and your
            session state to protect focus, not private content.
          </div>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="cf-faq-item" data-id="q8">
        <summary>
          What do Basic, Pro, and Limitless include?
          <span class="cf-faq-toggle" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
        </summary>
        <div class="cf-faq-body">
          <div class="cf-faq-content">
            Basic, or Free, covers core sessions, starter Shield protection,
            Goblin reactions, and progress foundations. Pro adds stronger
            Shield capacity, Manual Block, Planned Sessions, reminders,
            recovery nudges, and restore support. If a Limitless tier is offered
            later, its extras will be listed on pricing before checkout.
          </div>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="cf-faq-item" data-id="q9">
        <summary>
          What features are planned for later?
          <span class="cf-faq-toggle" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
        </summary>
        <div class="cf-faq-body">
          <div class="cf-faq-content">
            Planned features include Ghost Mode, DND-style quieting, uninstall
            protection, and advanced lock rules. They are planned for later and
            are not all live yet, so the app only promises what is available
            today.
          </div>
        </div>
      </details>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
